## 📌 Project Status

🚧 This project is currently under development.

The initial version focuses on collecting sensor data, monitoring plant conditions, and generating basic plant-care recommendations. Future versions will include improved machine learning models and automated watering.

---

## 🎯 Project Motivation

Plants are often damaged because of irregular watering, unsuitable temperature, or lack of monitoring.

The goal of this project is to develop a low-cost smart plant monitoring system that uses sensors and machine learning concepts to help users understand plant-care requirements.

---

## 🧠 Machine Learning Approach

The project uses sensor readings such as:

- Soil moisture
- Temperature
- Humidity

These readings can be used to classify plant conditions into categories such as:

- Needs Water
- Healthy
- Excess Water Risk
- Unfavorable Temperature

The initial model can be developed using Python and Scikit-learn. After testing, the model may be converted into a lightweight format suitable for embedded devices.

---

## 📊 Expected Output

The system is expected to:

1. Read real-time sensor data.
2. Monitor soil moisture and environmental conditions.
3. Identify possible plant stress conditions.
4. Display sensor readings.
5. Provide plant-care recommendations.
6. Trigger an LED or buzzer when attention is required.

---

## 🔬 Future Improvements

- Add an automatic water pump.
- Use a better capacitive soil-moisture sensor.
- Add an OLED display.
- Store sensor data in the cloud.
- Create a mobile dashboard.
- Train the model using real plant datasets.
- Add multiple plant profiles.
- Deploy a TinyML model directly on the ESP32.
- Add battery and solar-power support.

---

## ⚠️ Disclaimer

This project is intended for educational and experimental purposes.

The recommendations generated by the system may not always be accurate because plant requirements depend on plant species, soil type, weather, pot size, and other environmental conditions.

The system should not be considered a replacement for expert agricultural advice.

